  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#6399\", \"PowerToys#4566\"], \"answer\": \"A similar request has been filed before. PowerToys#6399 asked for PowerToys to pause itself automatically while a game is running. PowerToys#4566 asked for PowerToys Run to be disabled in full-screen or borderless apps. Neither ticket led to a general feature that detects heavy loads and turns modules off. What exists today is narrower. PowerToys Run has an 'Ignore shortcuts in full screen mode' setting, and there's a toggle to disable it. For everything else, turn off the modules you don't need in PowerToys Settings, or exit PowerToys while you game. If you want automatic per-app or per-load disabling across all modules, that is the part those tickets didn't cover. Add your use case to #6399 as a +1.\"}",
